  "title": "Henry Luce III Library – Central Philippine University Libraries",
  "text": "Henry Luce III Library – Central Philippine University Libraries Menu About Us Henry Luce III Library: History Who was Henry Luce III? Mission/Vision & Objectives Library Team Library Committee Contact Library Forms FAQs Sitemap Menu Home Library Services Newly Acquired Books College of Arts & Sciences College of Business & Accountancy College of Computer Studies College of Engineering College of Nursing College of Theology CPU Faculty-Authored Chat BERTHA Scanning Services Scholarly Publications Policy for outside researchers Online Resources Online Resources OPAC (Online Public Access Catalog) BAHÁNDÌAN Institutional Repository ProQuest eLibraryUSA by American Spaces Philippines EBSCO Information Services CPU LibGuides Open Access Databases Open Access eBooks Open Access Journals Library Sections Departmental Libraries Kindergarten Library Elementary Library Junior High School Library Senior High School Library College/Department Libraries Graduate School Library Theology Library Law Library HLL Sections Reference Section Reserve/Circulation Section Serials Section Filipiniana Section Meyer Asian Collection Technical Services Section American Corner Archives Knowledge for Development Center (KDC) Facebook X-twitter Youtube Instagram HENRY LUCE III LIBRARY It's not just about books. It's all about you. Institutional Repository BAHÁNDÌAN serves as Central Philippine University’s institutional repository, preserving and sharing digital materials representing the academic community’s scholarly work. Visit page Online Public Access Catalog Search the books and resources available in the library through the Library Catalog. Visit page Online Resources Check out all our available databases on the A-Z Database List on our LibGuides. Visit Page Our Other Online Resources FREE ONLINE RESOURCES FOR STUDENTS WITH SPECIAL NEEDS Free digital library that lets you borrow eBooks, audiobooks, and more. It’s a great way for students with special needs to access learning materials anytime, anywhere. easy-to-use app for OverDrive. It helps students with special needs by offering audiobooks, read-along books, and settings to change text size, color, and font. An open access journal offering a wide range of multi-disciplinary topics regarding education and services for individuals with disabilities. Funbrain offers hundreds of games, books, comics, and videos that develop skills in math, reading, problem-solving and literacy. Storyline Online streams videos featuring celebrated actors reading children’s books alongside creatively produced illustrations. Arcademics, formerly known as Arcademic Skill Builders, provides online educational video games that offer a powerful approach to learning basic math, language arts, vocabulary, and thinking skills. National library service for the blind and print disabled. Bookshare audiobooks and ebooks make reading easy. You can customize your reading experience with assistive reading features that remove reading barriers. ENGLISH LANGUAGE TEACHING (ELT) JOURNAL English Language Teaching Journal 2023 January Vol. 77 Issue 1 English Language Teaching Journal 2023 April Vol. 77 Issue 2 English Language Teaching Journal 2023 July Vol. 77 Issue 3 English Language Teaching Journal 2024 January Vol. 78 Issue 1 English Language Teaching Journal 2024 July Vol. 78 Issue 3 English Language Teaching Journal 2024 October Vol. 78 Issue 4 NEWLY ACQUIRED BOOKS College of Arts and Sciences College of Computer Studies College of Business and Accountancy College of Engineering College of Nursing College of Theology CPU Faculty-Authored Books This guide shows you how to access and use all the online resources and databases the Library is offering, and how to make the most of them for your study and research needs. Questions? Just Chat BERTHA by sending a message to our Facebook page or e-mail us at berthahll@cpu.edu.ph. Click to download LATEST NEWS AND UPDATES Events 𝐒𝐭𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐠𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐧𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐂𝐨𝐥𝐥𝐚𝐛𝐨𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧: 𝐓𝐚𝐤𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐒𝐜𝐡𝐨𝐨𝐥 𝐋𝐢𝐛𝐫𝐚𝐫𝐢𝐞